From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:39:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 199/207] dsv41 server: the compute default stays out of
 replies that cannot run a call

dashboard QA (one user message, no tools, max_tokens 64, thinking off)
scored 30/150 under TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1 against 140/150 with
it off: the default declared the built-in python tool in every chat, the
model called it, and the lane could not finish. With under 16 tokens left
the call never ran; when the result turn did not fit it ran and was not
inserted; max_tokens could also cut the call. Each reply ended at the
call: the stream hid it and said finish_reason tool_calls with no text,
the whole reply returned a python call the client never offered, and a
cut call stayed in content as DSML. The boot's trust guide, measured
inside thinking, also put `<expr> =` cells into thinking-off answers.

Under the default, a request that did not list code_interpreter now gets
the built-in tool only when its reply can run a call: no stop strings, no
logprobs or prompt_logprobs, no structured output, and max_tokens (or the
server's default) at least 1024. Otherwise it renders and runs as with
the default off; a no-tools logprobs request is no longer refused. A
built-in call the lane still cannot run never reaches such a client: it
leaves tool_calls and content, and the reply ends with finish_reason
length. Thinking-off chats get no boot guide under the default. A client
that lists code_interpreter, and every request with the default unset,
see no change.
